    TUI["Interactive Textual app<br/>streaming renderer · confirmations · HUD"]:::interface
    PIPE["Non-interactive runner<br/>deterministic stdout + exit semantics"]:::interface
    MODE{"Interaction contract"}:::decisionnode
    CHAT["chat<br/>read/discover + prose"]:::mode
    PLAN["plan<br/>read/discover + durable plan<br/>no mutation"]:::mode
    AGENTMODE["agent<br/>full governed execution"]:::mode
    USER_EVENT["MessageAction<br/>source=USER"]:::event

    USER_INPUT --> ENTRY --> CONFIG --> SURFACE
    SURFACE -->|yes| TUI --> MODE
    SURFACE -->|no| PIPE --> MODE
    MODE --> CHAT --> USER_EVENT
    MODE --> PLAN --> USER_EVENT
    MODE --> AGENTMODE --> USER_EVENT

    WHY_MODE["<b>WHY EXPLICIT CHAT / PLAN / AGENT MODES?</b><br/><b>Problem:</b> answering, planning, and mutating a machine have different social and safety contracts.<br/><b>Chosen:</b> one identity, memory, and ledger; tool availability and finish behavior vary by mode.<br/><b>Why not specialist agents:</b> handoffs duplicate context, lose rationale, and blur task ownership. Why not one unrestricted mode: read-only intent could cause side effects.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> continuity without role-transfer loss, with small mode-specific prompt/tool branches."]:::why
    WHY_WORKSPACE["<b>WHY A WORKSPACE-SCOPED DATA ROOT?</b><br/><b>Problem:</b> sessions, task state, indexes, and checkpoints must not collide across repositories or pollute source control.<br/><b>Chosen:</b> derive a stable workspace identity and store operational artifacts under the user data directory.<br/><b>Why not .grinta in every repo:</b> it dirties worktrees, risks accidental commits, and makes project permissions govern agent state.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> clean repositories and continuity per workspace; identity migration and path resolution require care."]:::why
    WHY_SURFACE["<b>WHY TWO PRESENTATION PATHS?</b><br/><b>Problem:</b> humans need incremental cards and confirmation dialogs; pipes and CI need stable text and process completion.<br/><b>Chosen:</b> both subscribe to the same semantic event stream but own separate rendering/lifecycle adapters.<br/><b>Why not make Textual pretend to be non-interactive:</b> terminal capabilities and blocking behavior differ fundamentally.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> honest automation and rich interaction; some presentation logic is duplicated."]:::why
  end

  USER_EVENT ==> EVENT_ASSIGN

  subgraph STAGE2["2 · RECORD THE FACT BEFORE ANY SUBSYSTEM REACTS — EVENT-SOURCED EVIDENCE PLANE"]
    direction LR
    EVENT_ASSIGN["EventStream.publish<br/>monotonic session ID · timestamp · source<br/>secret masking"]:::event
    EVENT_SERIAL["Serialize typed payload<br/>embedded ID + checksum"]:::event
    SQLITE_TX["Authoritative SQLite append<br/>BEGIN IMMEDIATE · INSERT only<br/>WAL journal · synchronous FULL"]:::durability
    PREDISPATCH["Arm pending Action after durable identity<br/><b>before inline delivery can produce an Observation</b>"]:::invariant
    DELIVERY{"Delivery policy"}:::decisionnode
    INLINE["Inline USER / CLI path<br/>same-stack causal ordering"]:::event
    QUEUE["Bounded worker queue<br/>backpressure metrics"]:::event
    SUBS["One fact, multiple projections<br/>controller · runtime · memory · UI"]:::event

    EVENT_ASSIGN --> EVENT_SERIAL --> SQLITE_TX --> PREDISPATCH --> DELIVERY
    DELIVERY --> INLINE --> SUBS
    DELIVERY --> QUEUE --> SUBS

    SQLITE_RULE["If SQLite append fails, <b>do not</b> fall back to event JSON.<br/>Two writable stores would create split-brain history."]:::invariant
    SQLITE_TX --> SQLITE_RULE

    WHY_APPEND["<b>WHY APPEND-ONLY EVENTS?</b><br/><b>Problem:</b> a mutable status row shows where the agent is, not which decision caused which side effect or what was known before failure.<br/><b>Chosen:</b> facts receive new IDs and are inserted once; corrections are later facts, never rewrites.<br/><b>Why not CRUD mutation:</b> updates erase intermediate states, complicate concurrent readers, and make crash timing indistinguishable from legitimate absence.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> temporal auditability, causal debugging, replay, and sequential writes; costs are log growth, projection code, schema evolution, and snapshots/indexes."]:::why
    WHY_ES["<b>WHY EVENT SOURCING, NOT MERELY LOGGING?</b><br/><b>Logging</b> describes work after hidden application state changed. <b>Event sourcing here</b> makes Action and Observation the contract from which controller state, UI, memory, audit, and recovery views are projected.<br/><b>Why not controller→runtime calls plus logs:</b> direct calls create a second invisible truth and couple each consumer to the caller.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> one causal vocabulary across control, execution, persistence, and presentation; ordering and projection consistency become explicit architectural duties."]:::why
    WHY_SQLITE["<b>WHY SQLITE AS THE AUTHORITATIVE LOCAL LEDGER?</b><br/><b>Workload:</b> one local writer, many readers, append-heavy records, long ordered scans, and crash recovery.<br/><b>Chosen:</b> per-session embedded transactions and indexes with no service process.<br/><b>Why not one JSON file per event:</b> directory/fsync overhead and expensive long scans. Why not Postgres/Redis: operational infrastructure exceeds a single-user tool’s needs.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> atomic local truth and simple deployment; locking/corruption risk is concentrated, so serialized writes, checksums, integrity checks, and explicit degraded health are required."]:::why
    WHY_WAL["<b>WHY WRITE-AHEAD LOGGING, AND WHICH WAL?</b><br/><b>Crash window:</b> the process may die after intent is accepted but before final data pages are durable.<br/><b>SQLite WAL:</b> changed pages enter a sequential journal before database checkpoint; readers keep a stable snapshot while the writer advances. FULL synchronous favors crash truth over maximum throughput.<br/><b>Legacy application WAL:</b> only with SQLite disabled, write .pending JSON before the canonical event file, then remove it; restart cleans or replays the marker.<br/><b>Why not silent fallback:</b> recovery cannot reason safely about two authorities.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> deterministic crash recovery at the cost of extra writes and checkpoint cleanup."]:::why
    WHY_PERSIST_FIRST["<b>WHY PERSIST BEFORE DELIVERY?</b><br/><b>Problem:</b> if a subscriber executes a tool and the process dies before its Action is durable, the workspace has an orphaned side effect.<br/><b>Chosen:</b> assign ID, sanitize, and persist first; then arm cause correlation and notify subscribers.<br/><b>Why not fire-and-forget persistence:</b> a small latency win is not worth unexplainable machine state.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> every dispatched action has durable lineage; storage latency enters turn latency."]:::why
    WHY_INLINE["<b>WHY INLINE DELIVERY FOR THE CONTROL-CRITICAL PATH?</b><br/><b>Problem:</b> an extremely fast runtime can emit an Observation before an asynchronously delivered Action has registered its pending cause.<br/><b>Chosen:</b> USER and single-session CLI delivery stays inline; higher-volume paths may use bounded workers.<br/><b>Why not thread-pool everything:</b> throughput would introduce a causality race exactly where ordering matters most.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> deterministic pending/cause correlation; slow inline subscribers can delay publication."]:::why
  end

  SUBS ==> STATE_PROJECT

  subgraph STAGE3["3 · PROJECT STATE AND SERIALIZE THE CONTROL PLANE"]
    direction LR
    STATE_PROJECT["Controller subscriber<br/>reduce events into AgentState + session state"]:::control
    STEP_REQ["step() request funnel<br/>call_soon_threadsafe to main loop<br/>integer counter preserves every wakeup"]:::invariant
    STEP_LOCK["One active inference step<br/>asyncio.Lock + bounded request drain"]:::control
    SERVICES["Focused orchestration services<br/>lifecycle · pending · retry · recovery<br/>stuck · safety · validation · routing"]:::control
    PENDING["Pending-action table<br/>Action.id ↔ Observation.cause"]:::invariant
    PREPARE["ContextPipeline.prepare_step<br/>project current ledger view"]:::context

    STATE_PROJECT --> STEP_REQ --> STEP_LOCK --> SERVICES --> PENDING --> PREPARE

    WHY_PROJECTION["<b>WHY PROJECT STATE FROM EVENTS?</b><br/><b>Problem:</b> the UI, controller, recovery logic, and audit need different views of the same run.<br/><b>Chosen:</b> keep immutable facts central and build purpose-specific current-state projections.<br/><b>Why not one giant mutable State object shared everywhere:</b> consumers would silently overwrite each other and restart could not prove how values were derived.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> replayable, testable reducers and independent read models; projection lag and reducer versioning must be managed."]:::why
    WHY_SERIAL["<b>WHY ONE STEP OWNER?</b><br/><b>Problem:</b> model calls are state transitions, not independent HTTP requests. Concurrent steps could read the same history, spend twice, and emit conflicting actions.<br/><b>Chosen:</b> all step requests enter the main asyncio loop; a counter prevents lost wakeups and a lock admits one inference step at a time.<br/><b>Why not recursive callbacks or one task per event:</b> they create cross-loop races and duplicate reasoning turns that look like model hallucination.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> causal clarity and deterministic spend; theoretical turn throughput is intentionally sacrificed."]:::why
    WHY_CAUSE["<b>WHY EXPLICIT ACTION→OBSERVATION CAUSE IDS?</b><br/><b>Problem:</b> parallel or delayed tools make temporal adjacency unreliable: the next observation is not necessarily the result of the previous action.<br/><b>Chosen:</b> Observation.cause carries the durable Action ID; pending state clears by identity, not position.<br/><b>Why not infer pairing from timestamps/order:</b> worker scheduling, retries, and streaming output break that assumption.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> exact latency, retry, barrier, and audit attribution; every runtime path must preserve correlation."]:::why
    WHY_SERVICES["<b>WHY A THIN ORCHESTRATOR OVER FOCUSED SERVICES?</b><br/><b>Problem:</b> lifecycle, retry, safety, pending work, and recovery interact but change for different reasons.<br/><b>Chosen:</b> SessionOrchestrator coordinates named services through a narrow OrchestrationContext facade.<br/><b>Why not a multi-thousand-line controller:</b> hidden cross-feature mutation makes local reasoning and testing impossible. Why not independent microservices: process/network boundaries add no value inside one local session.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> visible responsibilities and isolated tests; more modules and a facade that must resist becoming a service locator."]:::why
  end

  PREPARE ==> DISCOVER_TASK

  subgraph STAGE4["4 · GROUND THE TASK IN THE ACTUAL REPOSITORY — SELECTION BEFORE READING"]
    direction LR
    DISCOVER_TASK["Extract current task terms<br/>split camelCase · snake_case · paths<br/>remove generic coding stop words"]:::context
    FILE_ENUM["Enumerate source candidates<br/>git ls-files + untracked, else bounded walk<br/>ignore build/cache/vendor paths"]:::context
    FIRST_PASS["Deterministic first-turn signals<br/>explicit path mention · dirty file<br/>path/stem overlap · bounded rg content hits<br/>matching Python symbols"]:::context
    INDEX["Lazy workspace symbol index<br/>SQLite cache · hash + mtime freshness<br/>Tree-sitter; Python AST fallback"]:::context
    GRAPH["File import graph<br/>src file → imported workspace file"]:::context
    PERSONAL["Personalization prior per indexed file<br/>0.2 base + task score + entrypoint boost"]:::context
    PAGERANK["Personalized PageRank<br/>damping 0.85 · fixed 24 iterations<br/>normalize every iteration"]:::context
    COMBINE["Final rank<br/>graph centrality + task score + entrypoint boost<br/>deterministic path tie-break"]:::context
    RENDER_MAP["Token-bounded &lt;REPO_MAP&gt;<br/>ranked paths + up to 4 public signatures/file<br/>binary search maximum prefix fitting map_tokens"]:::context
    PREFLIGHT["First-turn &lt;CODING_PREFLIGHT&gt;<br/>top 6 candidates + reasons + dirty files<br/><b>hints only; verify before editing</b>"]:::context

    DISCOVER_TASK --> FILE_ENUM --> FIRST_PASS
    FILE_ENUM --> INDEX --> GRAPH --> PERSONAL --> PAGERANK --> COMBINE --> RENDER_MAP
    FIRST_PASS --> PERSONAL
    FIRST_PASS --> PREFLIGHT

    INDEX_INVALIDATE["Successful file mutation invalidates that path<br/>repo map cache marked dirty and lazily rebuilt"]:::invariant
    INDEX -. edit invalidation .-> INDEX_INVALIDATE -. next turn .-> RENDER_MAP

    WHY_RANK["<b>WHY RANK THE REPOSITORY AT ALL?</b><br/><b>Problem:</b> the whole repo rarely fits, but forcing the model to begin with blind glob/read loops wastes turns and may anchor on the wrong subsystem.<br/><b>Chosen:</b> provide a cheap structural prior: likely files and public symbols, never full contents.<br/><b>Why not inject the complete tree/content:</b> token cost grows with repo size and low-signal names crowd out task evidence. Why not provide nothing: every turn pays discovery latency and small models struggle to form a global map.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> faster orientation and architectural awareness; ranking can be wrong, so candidates are explicitly non-authoritative and source reads remain mandatory."]:::why
    WHY_SIGNALS["<b>WHY THESE FIRST-PASS SIGNALS?</b><br/><b>Explicit path mention</b> is highest-precision user intent. <b>Dirty files</b> represent the workspace’s active delta. <b>Path/stem overlap</b> captures naming conventions cheaply. <b>Bounded content hits</b> find concepts not encoded in filenames. <b>Matching symbols</b> provide a semantic breadcrumb without loading bodies.<br/><b>Why deterministic before embeddings:</b> zero model call, explainable scores, immediate startup, cross-language fallback, and stable tests.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> excellent lexical precision and predictable cost; synonyms and conceptual relationships can be missed."]:::why
    WHY_PAGE["<b>WHY PERSONALIZED PAGERANK ON IMPORTS?</b><br/><b>Problem:</b> lexical relevance finds files named like the task but misses architectural hubs, adapters, and dependencies that connect the change.<br/><b>Chosen:</b> import edges approximate dependency influence; PageRank propagates importance transitively, while task personalization teleports probability toward the current request.<br/><b>Why damping 0.85:</b> most weight follows architecture, while 15% restart prevents sinks/cycles from owning the ranking. <b>Why 24 iterations:</b> fixed bounded work gives stable practical convergence without a data-dependent latency tail.<br/><b>Why not degree count:</b> it sees only immediate neighbors. Why not pure semantic vectors: heavier, opaque, optional dependencies, and weaker explicit topology.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> task-focused structural centrality; dynamic imports and non-code relationships remain imperfect."]:::why
    WHY_ENTRY["<b>WHY BOOST ENTRYPOINTS AND ADD TASK SCORE TWICE?</b><br/><b>Entrypoint boost:</b> manifests, CLI/bootstrap files, and common roots explain how the system starts even when few files import them.<br/><b>Task score in personalization:</b> influences graph flow toward the task neighborhood. <b>Task score in the final sum:</b> preserves a direct relevance vote so a central but unrelated hub cannot dominate.<br/><b>Alternative rejected:</b> one opaque learned score that is difficult to debug or tune.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> an intentionally biased engineering heuristic—not a claim of mathematically pure ranking."]:::why
    WHY_MAP_BUDGET["<b>WHY PATHS + FOUR PUBLIC SIGNATURES UNDER A HARD TOKEN BUDGET?</b><br/><b>Paths</b> reveal module boundaries; <b>signatures</b> reveal available concepts and call surfaces; bodies would consume the budget before the model chooses what to inspect.<br/><b>Four symbols</b> caps per-file dominance. <b>Public-first</b> favors architectural API over implementation noise. <b>Binary search</b> finds the longest ranked prefix that fits without repeatedly trimming arbitrary text.<br/><b>Why not character truncation:</b> tokenizer density varies and a hard cut can split a structural entry.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> compact, syntactically intact orientation; private internals appear only after targeted reads."]:::why
  end

  RENDER_MAP ==> CONTEXT_BUDGET

  subgraph STAGE5A["5A · FIT HISTORY WITHOUT DESTROYING CAUSALITY — WINDOWING BEFORE COMPACTION"]
    direction LR
    CONTEXT_BUDGET["Resolve model capacity<br/>usable input = context window − output reservation<br/>subtract static prompt + tool schemas + context packet"]:::context
    LEDGER_VIEW["Project full durable history<br/>filter non-model events<br/>budget oversized tool results"]:::context
    TOKEN_EST["Tokenizer-aware event estimates<br/>model correction factor<br/>LRU cache by event fingerprint + rendering"]:::context
    PRESSURE{"Projected history exceeds<br/>token or event ceiling?"}:::decisionnode
    KEEP_ALL["No windowing<br/>preserve full projected history"]:::context
    PROTECT["Protect summaries / working set<br/>inject durable working set after compaction or restore"]:::context
    CHUNKS["Group causal chunks<br/>tool Action + matching Observation stay together"]:::context
    RECENT["Select newest whole chunks backward<br/>enforce minimum recent tool loops<br/>and minimum tail token floor"]:::context
    CEILING["If the newest required chunk alone is too large,<br/>truncate that copy to the remaining budget<br/>never mutate the ledger event"]:::invariant
    WINDOWED["Bounded prompt-history projection<br/>protected facts + intact recent causality"]:::context

    CONTEXT_BUDGET --> LEDGER_VIEW --> TOKEN_EST --> PRESSURE
    PRESSURE -->|no| KEEP_ALL --> WINDOWED
    PRESSURE -->|yes| PROTECT --> CHUNKS --> RECENT --> CEILING --> WINDOWED

    WHY_WINDOW["<b>WHY WINDOW BEFORE SUMMARIZING?</b><br/><b>Problem:</b> every transformation can lose information, and many over-budget moments can be solved by omitting old operational noise rather than inventing a new narrative.<br/><b>Chosen:</b> first build a reversible model-facing selection over the immutable ledger; compact only when sustained boundary pressure requires a new summary.<br/><b>Why not summarize on every turn:</b> added model latency/cost, semantic drift, and summaries of summaries. Why not raw tail truncation: it may remove the Action while retaining its Observation or erase durable anchors.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> cheap predictable pressure control with full audit history intact; older unselected detail is unavailable to that inference turn unless recalled."]:::why
    WHY_CAUSAL_WINDOW["<b>WHY CAUSAL CHUNKS, MINIMUM TOOL LOOPS, AND A TAIL FLOOR?</b><br/><b>Action/result pairing:</b> model APIs require coherent tool-call sequences and the result is meaningless without its request. <b>Minimum loops:</b> preserves enough recent think→act→observe examples for the model to know the current trajectory. <b>Tail token floor:</b> prevents many tiny protected events from crowding out the actual latest work.<br/><b>Why not keep the last N events:</b> N ignores token variance and can split pairs. Why not importance scoring here: selection must be deterministic, fast, and safe during emergency overflow.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> syntactically valid and operationally coherent prompts; some older high-value facts must survive through canonical state, summaries, or recall instead."]:::why
    WHY_TOKEN["<b>WHY MODEL-AWARE TOKEN BUDGETS WITH FIXED-PROMPT RESERVES?</b><br/><b>Problem:</b> the provider limit covers system text, tool schemas, dynamic context, history, and output—not history alone. Characters/token vary by model and by code/JSON density.<br/><b>Chosen:</b> derive usable input from model capability, reserve output, subtract measured fixed sections, apply catalog correction, and cache immutable event counts.<br/><b>Why not len(text)/4 only:</b> acceptable fallback, unsafe as the primary gate. Why not wait for provider rejection: overflow recovery occurs after latency and may lose the turn.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> proactive, model-portable limits; catalogs and estimates can still be conservative or stale."]:::why
    WHY_COPY["<b>WHY TRUNCATE A DEEP-COPIED VIEW AT SAFE BOUNDARIES?</b><br/><b>Problem:</b> trimming the durable Event object would make replay/audit depend on whichever model happened to need a smaller prompt. Cutting raw structured text can leave broken JSON/XML/tool envelopes that invite hallucinated continuation.<br/><b>Chosen:</b> copy model-facing events, prefer newline then whitespace cuts, add visible markers, and preserve opening/closing section tags.<br/><b>Why not invisible hard byte cuts:</b> they conceal missing evidence and corrupt structure.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> the model knows information is incomplete while the evidence plane remains lossless."]:::why
  end

  WINDOWED ==> COMPACT_GATE

  subgraph STAGE5B["5B · WHEN PRESSURE PERSISTS, COMPACT THE OLD OPERATIONAL ARC — CURRENT ACTIVE STRATEGY"]
    direction LR
    COMPACT_GATE{"Boundary tokens ≥ effective window<br/>− reserved summary − fixed prompt reserve<br/>or explicit /compact?"}:::decisionnode
    SKIP_COMPACT["Skip compaction<br/>also suppress same-turn double compact and<br/>recompact below last post-boundary size"]:::context
    PRUNE_SET["Active StructuredSummaryCompactor<br/>max_size 102; target roughly half-size history<br/>fold prior summary + older pruned events"]:::context
    DIGEST["Reduce source material before summarization<br/>group files · commands · errors · navigation<br/>plus last 5 non-user raw events"]:::context
    SUMMARY_INPUT["Compaction prompt<br/>durable task state is read-only authority<br/>goal context · latest verification · prior summary<br/>event digest · recent raw detail"]:::context
    SUMMARY_LLM["Same active LLM, plain prose completion<br/>budget min(5% context, 12k tokens)<br/>retry short/empty output up to configured repair attempts"]:::inference
    SUMMARY_ORDER["Required priority<br/>unresolved/blocking → next steps → failed approaches<br/>→ accomplished/architecture → decisions/rationale<br/>USER GOAL fallback only if durable task state absent"]:::context
    BOUNDARY["CondensationAction establishes a new boundary<br/>old raw events remain in ledger<br/>prompt projection becomes summary + recent tail"]:::event
    CONTINUITY["Canonical/fuzzy continuity comparison<br/><b>telemetry warning today; non-empty summary is accepted</b>"]:::warning

    COMPACT_GATE -->|no| SKIP_COMPACT --> BOUNDARY
    COMPACT_GATE -->|yes| PRUNE_SET --> DIGEST --> SUMMARY_INPUT --> SUMMARY_LLM --> SUMMARY_ORDER --> CONTINUITY --> BOUNDARY

    LEGACY_STRATS["Present in repository but not selected by current ContextPipeline:<br/>observation masking · recent-events · smart importance<br/>microcompact · composition pipeline"]:::optional

    WHY_COMPACT["<b>WHY A SUMMARY BOUNDARY INSTEAD OF DELETING EVENTS?</b><br/><b>Problem:</b> repeated windowing eventually hides too much of the operational arc for a fresh reasoning turn to understand how the present state emerged.<br/><b>Chosen:</b> synthesize older evidence into a bounded narrative checkpoint, then retain a raw recent tail; the immutable ledger still holds originals.<br/><b>Why not permanently rewrite history:</b> audit and postmortem truth would inherit summary errors. Why not keep unlimited raw context: cost, latency, attention dilution, and provider limits rise even with large windows.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> long-run continuity at bounded prompt cost; semantic loss is unavoidable and must be counterbalanced by deterministic state."]:::why
    WHY_ACTIVE["<b>WHY THE CURRENT SINGLE PROSE COMPACTOR, NOT THE LEGACY AUTO-SELECTOR?</b><br/><b>Chosen now:</b> one active mechanism with one trigger and one boundary contract; free prose lets the model allocate space to the actual session shape, while a strict section priority preserves resumability.<br/><b>Why not keep switching among masking, recency, semantic importance, and multi-layer pipelines:</b> policy became difficult to predict, test, and explain; a wrong strategy firing is itself context risk.<br/><b>Why not rigid schema output:</b> field compliance can consume attention and omit cross-cutting narrative. Deterministic task/canonical state already owns structured truth.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> simpler operations and richer narrative; prose is less machine-verifiable and the current continuity gate warns rather than vetoes."]:::why
    WHY_DIGEST["<b>WHY GROUPED DIGEST + FIVE RAW EVENTS?</b><br/><b>Grouped digest:</b> changes the evidence shape from thousands of repetitive lines into counts and unique files/commands/errors, reducing recency bias and prompt size 5–10× in intended workloads. <b>Five raw events:</b> retain exact local detail near the boundary where the next action depends on it.<br/><b>Why not send all pruned events to the summary model:</b> the summarizer can overflow or focus on late verbosity. Why not digest only: exact error/path detail disappears.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> macro arc plus a narrow microscope; details outside both survive only in the ledger/canonical reducers."]:::why
    WHY_SEPARATE_TRUTH["<b>WHY KEEP DURABLE TASK STATE OUT OF THE SUMMARY OUTPUT?</b><br/><b>Problem:</b> repeatedly copying objective, requirements, plan, and statuses into prose creates stale competing versions and goal drift.<br/><b>Chosen:</b> give durable task state to the compactor as read-only interpretation context, but re-inject the authoritative aggregate separately after compaction.<br/><b>Why not let the summary own task truth:</b> prose is lossy, model-generated, and replaced at every boundary.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> narrative memory can evolve while the task contract remains revisioned and inspectable."]:::why
  end

  BOUNDARY ==> PACKET_START

  subgraph STAGE5C["5C · RECONSTRUCT THE MINIMUM SUFFICIENT WORKING STATE — THE CONTEXT PACKET"]
    direction LR
    PACKET_START["Reduce events into deterministic CanonicalTaskState<br/>load revisioned TaskState + pre-compaction snapshot"]:::context
    P_USER["1 Recent user request context<br/>only preserved user turns absent from selected history<br/>section limit max(1,400 chars, 11% packet)"]:::context
    P_CONTRACT["2 Execution contract<br/>objective · requirements · constraints · plan/status · evidence<br/>limit: configured contract cap over max(1,800 chars, 18%)"]:::context
    P_SNAPSHOT["3 Compact snapshot<br/>only immediately after compaction<br/>restores files/tests/errors/decisions/background work<br/>section limit max(2,400 chars, 22%)"]:::context
    P_NEXT["4 Operational checkpoint<br/>next action + implementation checkpoint<br/>section limit max(1,200 chars, 11%)"]:::context
    P_CANON["5 Non-duplicated canonical details<br/>blockers · failed approaches · VCS · decisions<br/>processes · tests · dependencies<br/>renderer budget max(4,200 chars, 41%)"]:::context
    P_ACTIVE["6 Active tool/background status<br/>including output drained since last turn<br/>section limit max(900 chars, 7%)"]:::context
    P_SUMMARY["7 Latest narrative summary<br/>excluded if it is itself a packet/working-set marker<br/>section limit max(900 chars, 9%)"]:::context
    P_TAIL["8 Recent causal tail<br/>up to 10 non-message event details<br/>section limit max(1,200 chars, 14%)"]:::context
    PACKET["&lt;CONTEXT_PACKET&gt;<br/>ordered sections under character budget<br/>cached by events/state/snapshot fingerprint"]:::context

    PACKET_START --> P_USER --> P_CONTRACT --> P_SNAPSHOT --> P_NEXT --> P_CANON --> P_ACTIVE --> P_SUMMARY --> P_TAIL --> PACKET

    PACKET_BUDGET["Default 6,000 chars<br/>for ≥100k usable-token models: max(8k, min(32k, 4% of usable input))<br/>earlier sections win when total budget is exhausted"]:::invariant
    PACKET --> PACKET_BUDGET

    WHY_PACKET["<b>WHY A CONTEXT PACKET IN ADDITION TO HISTORY?</b><br/><b>Problem:</b> chronological history answers what happened; the next model turn needs an explicit answer to what is true now and what should happen next. Recovering state by rereading every event consumes attention and encourages stale facts.<br/><b>Chosen:</b> a bounded, deterministic current-state packet beside the causal tail.<br/><b>Why not replace history entirely:</b> state without evidence hides how conclusions were reached and removes local tool-call detail.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> state + trajectory are complementary inputs; duplicated facts must be actively suppressed."]:::why
    WHY_PACKET_FIELDS["<b>WHY EXACTLY THESE SECTIONS, IN THIS ORDER?</b><br/><b>User request</b> repairs intent lost by windowing. <b>Execution contract</b> defines completion truth. <b>Compact snapshot</b> restores the boundary immediately after loss. <b>Operational checkpoint</b> prevents restart hesitation. <b>Canonical detail</b> preserves blockers, decisions, failures, VCS, and tests. <b>Active status</b> prevents duplicate background commands. <b>Narrative summary</b> carries architectural arc. <b>Recent tail</b> provides local cause/effect.<br/><b>Ordering principle:</b> intent and obligation outrank narrative and recency when the packet cannot fit.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> the packet degrades toward task correctness rather than conversational completeness."]:::why
    WHY_BUDGET["<b>WHY A SMALL CHARACTER-BUDGETED PACKET WITH PERCENTAGE CAPS?</b><br/><b>Problem:</b> authoritative state can itself grow until it crowds out code, history, and tool schemas.<br/><b>Chosen:</b> 6k baseline with cautious scaling for very large contexts; each category has a cap and assembly stops low-priority expansion.<br/><b>Why characters here, tokens elsewhere:</b> sections are mostly bounded prose/state and character slicing allows structural safe-cut logic; the outer prompt still receives tokenizer-aware accounting.<br/><b>Why not equal shares:</b> categories have unequal failure cost—losing the objective is worse than losing old narrative detail.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> predictable control-plane overhead; a very complex task may require the external task store or targeted recall rather than a larger packet."]:::why
    WHY_TAGS["<b>WHY XML-LIKE MARKERS AND SAFE CLOSING TAGS?</b><br/><b>Problem:</b> dynamic data, old tool output, and user text can resemble instructions. Unclosed or silently clipped sections blur authority boundaries.<br/><b>Chosen:</b> typed markers such as CONTEXT_PACKET and EXECUTION_CONTRACT; truncation preserves both opening and closing tags and emits an explicit marker.<br/><b>Why not free-form concatenation:</b> models cannot reliably distinguish policy, state, evidence, and quoted source material.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> clearer prompt roles and easier inspection; tags are conventions, not a security sandbox, so runtime policy still enforces effects."]:::why
  end

