    WHY_MIDDLEWARE["<b>WHY DETERMINISTIC MIDDLEWARE AROUND A PROBABILISTIC MODEL?</b><br/><b>Problem:</b> prompting improves action selection but cannot guarantee cost, permission, safety, rollback, logging, or postcondition behavior.<br/><b>Chosen:</b> every tool proposal crosses an ordered execute/observe contract that can block before effects and reconcile after reality is known.<br/><b>Why not embed all policy in each tool:</b> rules drift and new tools bypass them. Why not prompt-only safety: a stochastic component cannot be the final authority over its own side effects.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> bounded blast radius and composable governance; middleware order is a compatibility contract and adds per-call overhead."]:::why
    WHY_ORDER_MW["<b>WHY DOES MIDDLEWARE ORDER MATTER?</b><br/><b>Safety/progress/cost/context first</b> reject actions that should never proceed. <b>Rollback before destructive execution</b> ensures recovery exists before mutation. <b>Pre-diff/autocheck/diagnostics</b> establish and verify edit consequences. <b>Index/file state</b> reconcile derived repository views. <b>Logging/telemetry/validation</b> record and judge the resulting observation.<br/><b>Alternative rejected:</b> unordered plugin hooks where a safety check can run after execution or a checkpoint after mutation.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> adding or moving middleware requires reasoning about temporal preconditions, not only feature ownership."]:::why
    WHY_PARALLEL["<b>WHY RESOURCE-AWARE BOUNDED PARALLELISM?</b><br/><b>Problem:</b> independent reads and distinct-file edits can reduce latency, but concurrent conflicting mutations destroy deterministic state and observation order.<br/><b>Chosen:</b> classify actions; allow safe read mixes and same-category distinct resource keys; serialize opaque MCP, conflicts, and mixed side-effect categories; cap each batch and wait for all cause IDs.<br/><b>Why not read-only parallelism only:</b> leaves safe distinct-resource throughput unused. Why not parallelize everything:</b> rollback, confirmation, prompts, and tests would observe races.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> speed where independence is provable; conservative serialization when identity or effects are opaque."]:::why
    WHY_CHECKPOINT["<b>WHY CHECKPOINT BEFORE RISKY ACTIONS, NOT AFTER EVERY EVENT?</b><br/><b>Problem:</b> rollback must capture the last known-good workspace before mutation; read-only commands add no recovery value and would flood retention.<br/><b>Chosen:</b> middleware snapshots non-trivial file edits, commands, and HIGH-risk future action types; trivial read-only commands are recognized and skipped.<br/><b>Why not after execution:</b> too late. Why not every step:</b> storage/time cost and a noisy checkpoint list. Why not only manual checkpoints:</b> humans cannot predict every bad autonomous action.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> transaction-like safety around effects; classification errors can over-snapshot or leave a gap, so HIGH-risk metadata provides a generic fallback."]:::why
  end

