    WHY_SHADOW["<b>WHY A PRIVATE CONTENT-ADDRESSED GIT STORE FOR WORKSPACE CHECKPOINTS?</b><br/><b>Problem:</b> checkpoints must handle modified/untracked/binary files, work without a clean user repo, deduplicate unchanged content, and restore any prior tree.<br/><b>Chosen:</b> pygit2 writes commits to a separate bare object store; a stat cache avoids rereading unchanged files; no subprocess or user branch is touched.<br/><b>Why not full directory copies:</b> O(repo size) data per checkpoint. Why not user Git commits/stash:</b> pollutes history, depends on repository state, and misses non-repo workspaces. Why not inverse patches:</b> fragile for deletes, binaries, renames, and command side effects.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> incremental cross-platform snapshots and branch independence; libgit2 storage/GC and whole-tree enumeration still cost resources."]:::why
    WHY_QUARANTINE["<b>WHY QUARANTINE EXTRA FILES DURING RESTORE?</b><br/><b>Problem:</b> restoring an exact snapshot normally deletes files created later, but those files may contain valuable user work or crash evidence.<br/><b>Chosen:</b> move extras into a timestamped checkpoint-local quarantine, then atomically replace snapshot files.<br/><b>Why not delete for perfect rollback:</b> rollback should reduce harm, not introduce irreversible loss. Why not leave extras in place:</b> the restored workspace would not match the checkpoint and tests could see mixed states.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> recoverable exactness; rollback consumes additional disk until quarantine is reviewed."]:::why
    WHY_LOCAL_RUNTIME["<b>WHY AN IN-PROCESS LOCAL RUNTIME INSTEAD OF MANDATORY DOCKER/RPC?</b><br/><b>Problem:</b> the default single-user agent needs low-latency access to the actual shell, editors, language servers, credentials, and OS paths.<br/><b>Chosen:</b> RuntimeExecutor lives in the process but communicates through typed Action/Observation events as if it were a boundary.<br/><b>Why not mandatory containers:</b> startup, mounts, path translation, daemon availability, nested virtualization, and environment mismatch harm local fidelity. Why retain typed boundaries: a future isolated driver remains possible and faults are attributable.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> native performance and easy debugging; runtime faults share the host process and policy cannot be advertised as isolation."]:::why
    WHY_FILE_API["<b>WHY A SMALL NATIVE FILE API WITH EXACT REPLACEMENT?</b><br/><b>Problem:</b> free-form patch/XML/JSON edits are easy for a model to almost format correctly and hard to make atomic across files.<br/><b>Chosen:</b> explicit paths; exact old→new anchors; create/replace/multiedit transactions implemented in code; reads/discovery remain separate.<br/><b>Why not shell redirection or a universal editor DSL:</b> escaping, encoding, partial writes, and ambiguous match behavior leak into model reasoning.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> deterministic failures and safer refactors; the model may need an extra read to obtain an exact anchor."]:::why
    WHY_INTEL["<b>WHY TREE-SITTER PLUS LSP?</b><br/><b>Tree-sitter</b> gives fast, local, cross-language structure for indexing even when a project cannot build. <b>LSP</b> gives compiler-aware definitions, references, diagnostics, and types when a language server is available.<br/><b>Why not LSP only:</b> server startup/configuration can fail and broad indexing would be expensive. Why not parsing only:</b> syntax cannot resolve dynamic/project-specific semantics.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> graceful structural baseline with optional semantic precision; two caches/invalidation paths must remain coherent."]:::why
  end

