    WHY_OBSERVE["<b>WHY ARE OBSERVATIONS FIRST-CLASS EVENTS?</b><br/><b>Problem:</b> an Action is only an intention; exit code, changed files, diagnostics, user denial, timeout, and external results determine reality.<br/><b>Chosen:</b> tools return typed, cause-linked Observations that are persisted and projected like Actions.<br/><b>Why not return raw values directly to the caller:</b> UI, retry, audit, context, and recovery would see different or incomplete outcomes.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> one evidence contract and exact latency/result attribution; observation schemas must represent partial and failed reality honestly."]:::why
    WHY_BARRIER["<b>WHY WAIT FOR THE WHOLE SCHEDULED BATCH?</b><br/><b>Problem:</b> prompting after the first of several parallel results makes the model reason from an intermediate world and potentially mutate a resource whose sibling action is still running.<br/><b>Chosen:</b> the next inference begins only after every cause-keyed pending action in the batch resolves or is classified.<br/><b>Why not stream each result into a new model turn:</b> more calls, nondeterministic context order, and race-amplified decisions.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> coherent batch snapshots and reproducible prompts; the slowest action sets batch latency."]:::why
    WHY_RETRY["<b>WHY CLASSIFIED BOUNDED RETRY INSTEAD OF CATCH-ALL RETRY?</b><br/><b>Problem:</b> transient transport/storage/tool failures may recover, but deterministic syntax, permission, and logic failures repeat cost and side effects.<br/><b>Chosen:</b> retry only known recoverable categories, with attempt limits/backoff; circuit and recovery services own escalation.<br/><b>Why not infinite self-healing:</b> liveness becomes an expensive loop. Why not fail immediately:</b> temporary faults would waste long session state.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> resilience with an explicit exhaustion boundary; taxonomy quality determines false retry/false failure rates."]:::why
    WHY_STUCK["<b>WHY DO ONLY HARD STUCK SIGNALS CONTROL THE LOOP?</b><br/><b>Problem:</b> legitimate TDD, exploration, and refactoring often look repetitive semantically; heuristic interruption can stop the agent exactly when iteration is useful.<br/><b>Chosen:</b> exact repeated action/observation/error sequences and monologue/null-action limits may stop or redirect; semantic similarity and cost-growth guesses remain telemetry.<br/><b>Why not an LLM judge every step:</b> added cost and another probabilistic veto over liveness.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> fewer false-positive stops; subtle waste may be detected later."]:::why
  end

