    EVIDENCE["Reviewable completion evidence<br/>task contract/status · test observations · diffs<br/>files/checkpoints · full causal ledger"]:::durability
    OUTPUT --> EVIDENCE

    WHY_FINISH["<b>WHY IS THE FINAL MODEL MESSAGE THE LIFECYCLE BOUNDARY?</b><br/><b>Problem:</b> the user needs one observable event that means the agent has stopped acting. A hidden validator veto previously risked leaving the controller RUNNING with no next action.<br/><b>Chosen:</b> explicit final prose is persisted, then FINISHED is published immediately.<br/><b>Why not infer completion from silence or an empty tool queue:</b> both can occur during failure or waiting. Why not a separate mandatory finish tool:</b> plain response semantics already exist in chat/plan and providers; another tool creates a failure mode after work is done.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> clear liveness and UI behavior; the model may still finish prematurely."]:::why
    WHY_ADVISORY["<b>WHY IS COMPLETION VALIDATION ADVISORY TODAY?</b><br/><b>Problem:</b> tests/diffs/task evidence are valuable, but no single validator reliably knows user intent, environment constraints, or whether a warning deserves another autonomous mutation.<br/><b>Chosen:</b> validators collect an independent quality signal after the final boundary and emit a durable warning.<br/><b>Why not a hard veto without a recovery transition:</b> it creates a non-terminal state with no actor responsible for the next step. A future hard gate would need an explicit reopen/replan protocol and bounded authority.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> liveness and evidence are separated; correctness is reviewable, not guaranteed by the state enum."]:::why
    WHY_EVIDENCE["<b>WHY SEPARATE EVIDENCE COLLECTION, QUALITY SIGNALING, AND LIFECYCLE AUTHORITY?</b><br/><b>Evidence</b> records what happened. <b>Validation</b> interprets whether evidence looks sufficient. <b>Lifecycle</b> decides whether more actions may occur.<br/><b>Why not collapse them:</b> a missing test result should not silently erase history, and a warning should not mutate the workspace without an accountable control transition.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> interview-defensible boundaries and safer future evolution; users must understand that FINISHED means execution ended, not mathematical proof of correctness."]:::why
  end

  OUTPUT ==> DONE

  subgraph OBSERVABILITY["CROSS-CUTTING · THE MODEL VIEW MAY SHRINK; THE OPERATOR TRACE DOES NOT"]
    direction LR
    DONE["Run closed"]:::phase
    HUD["Live HUD<br/>mode · model · state · context/tokens · cost<br/>runtime · MCP/skills · persistence health"]:::interface
    CARDS["Event-derived cards<br/>actions · observations · diffs · confirmations<br/>errors · task state · compaction"]:::interface
    LOGS["Session-scoped structured logs<br/>prompt section metrics · latency · tool/persistence counters"]:::reliability
    AUDIT["Append-only trajectory / audit export<br/>postmortem does not depend on final prose"]:::durability

    SUBS -. render every durable fact .-> HUD
    SUBS -. semantic event cards .-> CARDS
    PIPELINE -. execution telemetry .-> LOGS
    SQLITE_TX -. complete trace .-> AUDIT

    WHY_OBS["<b>WHY LOCAL EVENT-DERIVED OBSERVABILITY?</b><br/><b>Problem:</b> agent failures are often contextual—wrong file, lost goal, repeated tool loop—not ordinary exceptions. The operator needs to reconstruct what the model saw and what the machine did.<br/><b>Chosen:</b> metrics, cards, audit, and logs are projections of the same local event/evidence plane; prompt compaction never deletes the operator trace.<br/><b>Why not cloud-only telemetry:</b> source, commands, paths, and outputs may be private; network availability should not determine debuggability. Why not raw logs only:</b> humans need semantic grouping and live progress.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> privacy-aligned postmortems and trust; local retention, redaction, and disk usage remain product responsibilities."]:::why
  end

