    STACK_GIT["pygit2 / libgit2<br/>private content-addressed rollback"]:::foundation
    STACK_EXT["Native tools + MCP<br/>stable core · replaceable edge"]:::foundation

    WHY_LOCAL["<b>WHY LOCAL-FIRST?</b><br/><b>Problem:</b> coding depends on the exact checkout, uncommitted files, toolchain, credentials, processes, and OS behavior.<br/><b>Chosen:</b> keep control, execution, history, checkpoints, and UI on the developer machine; only configured LLM/MCP calls leave it.<br/><b>Why not hosted-first:</b> repo mirroring creates state drift, privacy exposure, latency, tenancy infrastructure, and a second environment that may not reproduce the bug.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> high fidelity and user-owned evidence; execution shares the user trust domain, so policy, confirmation, rollback, and honest sandbox labeling are mandatory."]:::why
    WHY_PYTHON["<b>WHY PYTHON WITH NATIVE-BACKED HOT PATHS?</b><br/><b>Problem:</b> model SDKs and AI integrations evolve faster than the product can afford binding lag.<br/><b>Chosen:</b> Python for orchestration and contributor velocity; C/Rust-backed parsing, tokenization, serialization, Git, and package resolution where throughput matters.<br/><b>Why not a Rust rewrite:</b> stronger static guarantees are attractive, but provider lag, FFI work, and contributor cost dominate now.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> fast adaptation in exchange for disciplined boundaries, profiling, and explicit concurrency control."]:::why
    WHY_TUI_TECH["<b>WHY TEXTUAL/RICH AS THE PRESENTATION STACK?</b><br/><b>Problem:</b> long agent runs need incremental components, keyboard control, live metrics, diffs, and confirmations without leaving the terminal.<br/><b>Chosen:</b> Textual supplies a stateful async widget/application model; Rich supplies mature terminal rendering primitives.<br/><b>Why not hand-written ANSI:</b> focus, resize, layout, and platform behavior become product code. Why not a browser frontend:</b> Node/server/IPC packaging exceeds the local workflow need.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> a real operational UI from Python; terminal capability variance and Textual-specific lifecycle complexity remain."]:::why
    WHY_PACKAGE_TECH["<b>WHY JSON SETTINGS, UV ENVIRONMENTS, AND HATCHLING BUILDS?</b><br/><b>JSON:</b> strict ubiquitous interchange for CLI, schemas, automation, and model-readable configuration. <b>uv:</b> fast reproducible bootstrap/resolution without making its environment wrapper the product runtime. <b>Hatchling:</b> small standards-based wheel/sdist backend.<br/><b>Why not one all-owning packaging framework or custom config DSL:</b> environment management, build publication, and user configuration have different responsibilities.<br/><b>Consequence:</b> replaceable boring layers and fast onboarding; JSON sacrifices comments and uv remains an external developer tool."]:::why
  end
